// This file tracks known vulnerabilities that are accepted or mitigated.
//
// As of issue #867, the canonical waiver format is `.vulnignore.yml`. This
// file is kept as a flat ID list so legacy tools (and the codebase's
// pre-issue-#867 govulncheck step) keep working without reading YAML.
//
// When you add a new waiver, also add it to .vulnignore.yml with the
// structured justification, mitigation, expires_on, and approved_by fields.
//
// CI enforcement of the expires_on date lives in
// .github/workflows/security.yml → action-pinning.

GO-2026-4316
